+/* ---- null GL -------------------------------------------------------------
+   With the glue driving the fabric, Mesa's output never reaches the screen:
+   every frame the fabric shows is built by libmisterglue from the GL calls it
+   shadows. Mesa then only costs memory and time, and llvmpipe keeps binning
+   work into a scene nothing ever flushes -- 64 KiB data blocks at ~1.4 MB/min
+   of attract mode (PLAN.md 1l). With SDL_MISTER_NULL_GL on (the default when
+   SDL_MISTER_GLUE is set; =0 keeps Mesa) no EGL or GL library is loaded: GL
+   entry points resolve to the glue's wrappers, which forward to the stubs
+   below. Queries replay what Mesa llvmpipe answered on the device for a GLES2
+   context (work/glcaps.c); object names are unique counters; compile, link
+   and framebuffer status succeed; everything else is a no-op returning 0.
+   After cash.cow.dx-mister's drivers/gles3/mister_null_gl.cpp. */
